  551              /---------------------------------------------------------
  552              /LOOP TO RECEIVE THE NEXT 128 8-BIT XMODEM BYTES, AND SAVE
  553              /THEM IN THE NEXT 128*2/3 12-BIT BUFFER WORDS, COMPUTING
  554              /THE CHECKSUM AS WE GO. EACH 3 XMODEM BYTES BECOMES TWO
  555              /12-BIT BUFFER WORDS, ENCODED AS FOLLOWS
  556              /(DEC-S8-OSSMB-A-D PAGE 5-3, ITEM 11):
  557              /
  558              /           0        3  4                         11
  559              /          ------------ ----------------------------
  560              /  WORD 1 |BYTE 3 <0:3>|        BYTE 1 <0:7>        |
  561              /          ------------ ----------------------------
  562              /  WORD 2 |BYTE 3 <4:7>|        BYTE 2 <0:7>        |
  563              /          ------------ ----------------------------
  564              /ON ENTRY:
  565              /  AC=0
  566              /  CHKSUM=0
  567              /  XBCOUNT=-128
  568              /  BUFPTR=ADDRESS OF NEXT BUFFER WORD
  569              /  BUF123=0 FOR BYTE 1
  570              /         1 FOR BYTE 2
  571              /        -1 FOR BYTE 3
  572              /ON EXIT:
  573              /  (SEE ABOVE COMMENT)
  574              /---------------------------------------------------------
  575 00445  4334  XRDLUP, JMS     TPIN    /GET BYTE INTO AC AND RXBYTE
  576 00446  1325          TAD     CHKSUM
  577 00447  3325          DCA     CHKSUM
